  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "Daily Nous nalunaarpoq Journal of Medical Ethics-imut nassiunneqarsimasoq, kingorna piiaanneqarsimasoq, taaguutinik AI-mit sioqquserneqarsimasunik amerlasuunik ilaqartoq — universitetinut ilaqutigiiffiusuupput sioqquserlutik allaqqasunillu allagartaatinut atorsimanngitsunik — allattup nassiussimasaa naammattumik iluinnaq aaqqinngisimasagaluarluni ilusilersorneqarnissamut periarfissaqarluni. Allaaserisap tamanna naligiissitaraa Bioethics-imut, taaguutit misissuinerata programmikkut ingerlanneqartup ajornartorsiutimik nassaartitsisinnaagaluartoq, oqaatigalugulu naammattumik ajornartorsiuteqartoq tassaanngitsoq nassaartitsinermut teknologiit (isummersuisumit ataasip programmia taaguutit sioqquserneqarsimasut minutimut ikinnerusumi nassaartippai), kisianni ilusilersuisunut akiliisoqannginnera aammalu saqqummiussivinnut kajumissaarutit amerlanertaanissamik misissuinermit annertunerusumik ilinniagassiussisarnerat.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Paasissutissanik akeqanngitsumik atuisarneq billioninik dollarinillu naliliisarnerit AI-p",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "Demis Hassabis siunnersuutigaa FINRA-tut naalakkersuisoqarnissaa siulersuutaasumik modellit saqqummiunneqarnerinut: misissuisarfiit modellit misissorneqarnissaannut nassiussagaat ulloq 30-t missaani saqqummiunneqarnissaannut siornagut, aallaqqaammut nammineq akuerisamik, kingusinnerusukkut Amerika Naalagaaffiit niuerfianni piumasaqaataasumut ingerlaqqilluni.",
  "Denied": "Akuerinngilaq",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Politikkimut aallaqqaataasumik atuutilersinneqarsinnaasoq",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Politikkimut aallaqqaataasumik atuutilersinneqarsinnaasoq /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip-imi — nittartagaq annikitsoq allanngoqattaartuunngitsoq, naatsorsuutinit atuarneqarsinnaasumik immikkoortumik tamakkiisumik ilaqartoq, Cloudflare Pages-imut imaluunniit allanngoqattaartuunngitsumik hostingimut piareersimasoq.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Naatsorsuutinit atuarneqarsinnaasumik politikkinik nittartakkanni atuutilersitsineq",
  "Disclaimer": "Apeqqutigineqarsinnaasoq",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "Inunnut sammivittaasumik UI-mit, SEO-mit, imaluunniit naliginnaasunik API-nit assigiinngitsumik, AI Ingestion & Capability Layer nittartakkanut naatsorsuutinut sammivittaasumik sanaartornermik tunniussivoq: Manifest Immikkoortoq (iserfiit soorlu /llms.txt aamma /ai/manifest.json), Corpus Immikkoortoq (naatsorsuutinit atuarneqarsinnaasumik ilisimasat), Piginnaanermut Immikkoortoq (agentinit atorneqarsinnaasut atortut), aammalu Naalakkersuinermut Immikkoortoq (qanoq pigisaanerat, akuersissuteqarneq, versioneqarneq). Aallaqqaammut static-imik ingerlatsivoq, API-nulli MCP-mullu qaffasinnerusumut allanngortinneqarsinnaasumik. Naotsorsuut: allaaserisami matumani AICL-ip taaguutigaa misissorneqarnermut sanaartorneq; nittartakkami una protokollimut qupperniniililu AICL AI-p Imaanut Akuersissuteqarnermut Immikkoortumut tunngavoq.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "Allattorsimaffiit",
  "Docs / Examples": "Allattorsimaffiit / Assersuutit",
  "Document library": "Allattorsimaffiit katersugaasiat",
  "Does AI have rights — and which framings are even coherent?": "AI pisinnaatitaaffeqarpa — sunallu isigineqarnerit paasisimaarluartunngortarnerat?",
  "Download": "Aallussineq",
  "Draft status": "Aallaqqaataasup statusia",
  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "Ilinniartitsinermut misilitsiniaq: HMAC-SHA256 isumaannaammik peqatigiiffiusumik atorlugu, aperiuteqarnermut naapertuuttunik, piffissamik killeqartunik, misissorneqarsinnaasunillu akuersissummik tokeninik takutitsisumik. Atuuttumi tokenit assimmigalutinngitsumik atsiorneqartariaqarput, saqqummiussisup pisinnaatitaaffii ammasoq /.well-known/-mi nassaartinneqarsinnaalluni.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "/topics-imut ilaanngussat arfineq-pingasut nutaat, matumani AI agentimit misissorneqartut, assilinerluni katersorneqartinnagit — malittarisassaq siornatigut assigalugu: oqaasertaqarfik tamarmik pisortaqarfiusoq aallussineqarsimalluni uppernarsarneqarsimallunilu, killiffigineqartallu nammineq allaaserisatut, ilanngunneqannginnerani. Katillugit ilaanngussat 14-t.",
  "Email": "E-mail",
  "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model": "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model",
  "Empirical Research": "Misissuinikkut Ilisimatusarneq",
  "English edition →": "Tuluttut immikkoortoq →",
  "Ensure openness is machine-executable — so goodwill is not discarded as legal uncertainty.": "Ammaneq naatsorsuutinit atortoqarsinnaasuulersillugu qulakkeerneqassaaq — taamaalilluni kajumissuseq inatsisitigut naammagittaalliornermut peeqqutaanavianngitsoq.",
  "Epistemology": "Ilisimasat pillugit ilisimatuussutsi",
